<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Jobst of Moravia</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1351–1411</span> · Also known as Jodok of Moravia</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Jobst of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/moravia">Moravia</a> was margrave of Moravia from 1375 and a member of the Luxembourg dynasty, a nephew of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/charles-iv">Emperor Charles IV</a>. Rich and ambitious, he took part in the struggles among the Luxembourgs and acquired <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/brandenburg">Brandenburg</a> in 1388. In 1410 he was elected King of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/roman-empire">Romans</a> in rivalry with his cousin Sigismund, but died a few months later in 1411.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/jobst-of-moravia.jpg" alt="Jobst of Moravia" width="261" height="436" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: AnonymousUnknown author · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Jo%C5%A1t_Lucembursk%C3%BD.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
